<title>SWEDEN: FINNISH AIRPORTS MOVE 10.2 PCT MORE CARGO IN SEPT.</title>
<headline>FINNISH AIRPORTS MOVE 10.2 PCT MORE CARGO IN SEPT.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish airports handled 10.2</p>
<p>percent more cargo and 8.2 percent more mail in September this</p>
<p>year compared to September 1995, Finland's civil aviation</p>
<p>authority said on Monday.</p>
<p>The authority said for the first nine months of 1996 cargo</p>
<p>volumes rose by 4.7 percent versus the same 1995 period while</p>
<p>mail volumes jumped 17.0 percent.</p>
<p>It released the following data about airport activity.</p>
<p>				   SEPT 1996		  YR TO DATE</p>
<p>			    Total   Pct change     Total   Pct change</p>
<p> Cargo (in tonnes)     7,951  10.2	     64,823     4.7</p>
<p> Mail  (in tonnes)     1,578   8.2	     13,480    17.0</p>
<p> Landings		 23,908  -1.4	    213,840    -2.5</p>
<p> Passengers	    927,750   6.0	  7,929,567     8.6</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
